# Audience: desktop + iOS Safari

Owner lesson (**Nov 2026** — Type condition chips): Cursor/Chrome **device toolbar** looked fine while **real iPhone Safari** on live Railway showed the grey value bar shifted up. Blink ≠ WebKit.

## Hard rule

1. **Primary clients** = **desktop browsers** and **iOS Safari** (many users). Treat both as ship gates for UI layout.
2. **Chrome / Cursor “mobile view” is not iOS.** It can hide WebKit-only bugs (flex + nested `height`/`line-height`, font metrics, Teko optical pads).
3. Do **not** tell the owner a phone UI issue is fixed after only local Chrome device emulation.
4. For detail chips / tag composites / locked-height HUD rows: prefer **font-agnostic** flex centering; avoid nested `height`/`line-height: var(--tag-h)` inside a `--tag-h` flex child (iOS shifts the paint box).
5. Still honor `verify-live-before-fixed.mdc`: local-only vs **deployed** Safari on `ggendb.up.railway.app` must be stated honestly.
6. **Type condition tip (owner confirmed iOS Nov 2026):** padded CDN plate + webp stretch ≠ fixed. Proven path = CSS solid + `clip-path` tip (see `tag-composite-plates.mdc`). Playwright **WebKit** iPhone viewport is a useful stand-in while iterating; **owner’s real iPhone Safari** is still the final gate before saying “fixed on iOS.” Do not claim phone-fixed from desktop Cursor preview alone.

## When touching UI that ships to phones

| Check | Enough? |
|---|---|
| Desktop local / live | needed |
| Chrome device mode only | **not** enough for “works on phone” |
| Playwright WebKit iPhone viewport | good while iterating; not a substitute for owner device |
| Real iOS Safari (owner device) after deploy | required before “fixed on phone” |

